  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` conflicts with ARCH-4.\n\n**Why I stopped**\n- `OrderPlaced` (schemaVersion 3) is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which are in other repositories.\n- ARCH-4 says changes must be additive, and removals must go through deprecation.\n- \"Nothing reads it anymore\" is true for this repo. I can't check whether those two consumers read `channel`. If either does, dropping it from the event would break it.\n\n**What I'd propose instead**\n1. **Now:** mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on `OrderPlaced`, and keep emitting it. Optionally make it optional in the request, with a default, so clients can stop sending it.\n2. **After the consumers confirm they don't use it:** remove it in a new schema version (v4), and coordinate the cutover with billing-service and analytics-ingest.\n3. **Order model:** `channel` can only come out of the model once the event no longer needs it. `orderPlaced()` copies it from `order.channel`. The model change would also remove the `channel` validation and the `channel` request field. That changes the `POST /orders` contract for any client that sends it.\n\n**Decision for you:** do you want me to do step 1 now (deprecate and keep emitting)? Or have the consumer teams already confirmed they don't read `channel`? If so, tell me and I'll do the full removal as a v4 event.",
